{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121340","id":4047672007,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7xQpLH","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121340","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121340.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121340.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121340","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121340/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121340/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121340/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/88140eec56e26f3a7d62b0934aea94bc215d2fd9","number":121340,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Prevent crash when `CameraFeed.get_texture_tex_id` is passed a value out of `FeedImage` range.","user":{"login":"Rhombert","id":30680078,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjgwMDc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30680078?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rhombert","html_url":"https://github.com/Rhombert","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rhombert/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rhombert/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rhombert/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rhombert/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rhombert/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rhombert/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rhombert/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rhombert/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rhombert/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #121266 \r\n\r\nRoot cause, as far as I could find, is that there's no validation on the p_which arg of CameraFeed::get_texture_tex_id. To resolve this I:\r\n- Added a helper function that confirms whether or not a given value is valud for the `FeedImage` enum.\r\n- Added an `ERR_FAIL` macro that checks against the new helper, and has the function return a default value of `0` if the `p_which` value is invalid.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nRoot cause, as far as I could find, is that there's no validation on the p_which arg of CameraFeed::get_texture_tex_id. To resolve this I:\r\n- Added a helper function that confirms whether or not a given value is valud for the `FeedImage` enum.\r\n- Added an `ERR_FAIL` macro that checks against the new helper, and has the function return a default value of `0` if the `p_which` value is invalid.\r\n\r\nTested manually with on linux with the scons args helpfully provided by qarmin:\r\n`scons -j$(nproc) platform=linuxbsd target=editor arch=x86_64 dev_build=yes use_asan=yes debug_symbols=yes optimize=none`\r\n\r\nThe error I added appears in the expected cases, and the heap-buffer-overflow error no longer appears whatsoever. Performed two out of range tests with integers, all three in range tests with integers, and enum tests with `RGBA` and `CBCR`.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097326,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTczMjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:linuxbsd","name":"platform:linuxbsd","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":410064485,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw0MTAwNjQ0ODU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/needs%20testing","name":"needs testing","description":"","color":"ffcc44","d